WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:05.447
At this stage think of Python as a tool that follows
instructions in order We

00:00:05.474 --> 00:00:12.677
provide values Python stores them performs
operations on them and gives us a result For

00:00:12.690 --> 00:00:17.032
example imagine that we have sales of one thousand
dollars and costs of eight hundred

00:00:17.059 --> 00:00:22.680
dollars Python can store those two values and
calculate profit by subtracting costs

00:00:22.706 --> 00:00:28.246
from sales The calculation is simple but the
important idea is that the process

00:00:28.272 --> 00:00:33.997
is repeatable In real analytics work the same
pattern can be applied

00:00:34.010 --> 00:00:39.618
to thousands or millions of records Later in the
course libraries such as NumPy

00:00:39.644 --> 00:00:44.750
and Pandas will help us work with larger datasets
For now we are learning the

00:00:44.763 --> 00:00:48.000
small building blocks that those larger workflows
depend on
